      "page_idx": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Expressions Using Letter-Numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.085,
            0.826,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": "？ How much should she pay if she buys 10 coconuts and 5 kg jaggery?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.117,
            0.474,
            0.136
          ],
          "content": "Cost of 10 coconuts = 10 × ₹35"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.136,
            0.465,
            0.155
          ],
          "content": "Cost of 5 kg jaggery = 5 × ₹60"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.155,
            0.68,
            0.174
          ],
          "content": "Total cost  = 10 \\times \\bar{x}35 + 5 \\times \\bar{x}60 = \\bar{x}350 + \\bar{x}300 = \\bar{x}650.",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.182,
            0.815,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "？ How much should she pay if she buys 8 coconuts and 9 kg jaggery?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.224,
            0.848,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": "？ Write an algebraic expression to find the total amount to be paid for a given number of coconuts and quantity of jaggery."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.274,
            0.811,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "Let us identify the relationships and then write the expressions."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.304,
            0.814,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": "| Quantity needed | Relationship | Expression |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Cost of coconuts | Number of coconuts × 35 | c × 35 |\n| Cost of jaggery | Number of kgs of jaggery × 60 | j × 60 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_table_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.461,
            0.847,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": "Here, ‘c’ represents the number of coconuts and ‘j’ represents the number of kgs of jaggery. The total amount to be paid will be:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.33,
            0.503,
            0.667,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": "Cost of coconuts + Cost of jaggery."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.527,
            0.733,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": "The corresponding algebraic expression can be written as:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.551,
            0.571,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": "c \\times 35 + j \\times 60",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.586,
            0.847,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": "Use this expression (or formula) to find the total amount to be paid for 7 coconuts and 4 kg jaggery."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.635,
            0.847,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": "Notice that for different values of ‘c’ and ‘j’, the value of the expression also changes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.673,
            0.666,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": "Writing this expression as a sum of terms we get:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.411,
            0.695,
            0.588,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": "\\boxed { \\quad c \\times 3 5 \\quad } + \\quad \\boxed { \\quad j \\times 6 0 \\quad }",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.723,
            0.847,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 4:** We are familiar with calculating the perimeters of simple shapes. Write expressions for perimeters."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.768,
            0.847,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "The perimeter of a square is **4 times the length of its side**. This can be written as the expression: **4 × q**, where q stands for the sidelength."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.814,
            0.847,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": "？ What is the perimeter of a square with sidelength 7 cm? Use the expression to find out."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.864,
            0.849,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": "You must have realised how the use of letter-numbers and algebraic expressions allows us to express general mathematical relations in"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.812,
            0.938,
            0.84,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": "83"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
